rights, and do not restrict statutory exceptions or independent works.

5. Termination. Breach terminates the permissions granted here. On the first
written notice from a rights holder, complete cure within thirty days restores
the relevant permissions. Repeated or uncured breaches require written
reinstatement. Compliant recipients do not automatically lose their own rights
because of a distributor's breach. Legal liability is not waived.

6. Disclaimer. To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, the software
is supplied as-is without warranties of merchantability, fitness, title,
noninfringement, accuracy, availability or compatibility. Rights holders and
contributors are not liable for software-related damages, including text
replacement, data loss, API charges, interruption or indirect loss. Mandatory
